%% Duet: the one behavior graph of the person's health app (started 2026-10-25).
%% The graph is the spec; Verus derives from it. It states the ideal behavior of the full
%% product for every person, from Dev's intent and the settled sources, never from existing
%% code. decisions.md holds the charter, the sources and the dated decisions it cites.
%% Written region by region; this file currently holds your screens, the thread and its alerts, notes and medications you enter, the account and export, your health sources, the conversation, follow-through, Duet's own work and Today, For my doctor, your practice, and what comes back from it.
%% Scope: MVP behavior (Dev 2026-10-25); later functionality joins as connected graphs.
%%
%% Events. Every labeled step carries a declared event: who causes it, what it needs, and
%% what it is for.
%% events declared
%% event sign in | by you | needs not ADeleting | reason: an account being deleted takes no new sessions (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You sign in on this device: Sign in with Apple or email on iPhone, Google or email on Android, email on the web (ENG-161, Dev 2026-10-20). Whatever the method, a person has one account; a first sign-in creates it, and nothing about your health is kept before it (ENG-111).
%% event agree and continue | by you | command on your setup: Agree and continue, clicked while DIn | needs AAgree | reason: only your own agreement on this device records the Terms | You agree to the current Terms after signing in; Duet records that version and when (north-star.md, Identity and setup). Duet then asks for a display name only when your sign-in brought none.
%% event save your display name | by you | command on your setup: Save name, clicked while DIn | needs AName | reason: the name is yours to give | You give Duet the name it uses for you; it is never verified.
%% event change your display name | by you | command on your account: Change name, clicked while DIn | needs AReady, TCur | reason: the name is yours to change; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You change the name Duet uses for you, at any time; it is never verified, and Duet holds no legal name (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event allow AI | by you | command on your setup: Allow AI, clicked while DIn | needs AChoose | reason: AI permission is your choice | You allow Duet's AI for conversation, its private memory of you, and its own work, after reading what it does and its limits (north-star.md, Privacy; ENG-161 standing notice).
%% event not now for AI | by you | command on your setup: Not now, clicked while DIn | needs AChoose | reason: AI permission is your choice | You decline Duet's AI for now; everything that isn't AI keeps working.
%% event allow AI in settings | by you | command on your AI settings: Allow AI, clicked while DIn | needs PNot, TCur | reason: AI permission is your choice; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You give Duet's AI permission later, from settings.
%% event withdraw AI permission | by you | command on your AI settings: Withdraw permission, clicked while DIn | needs PAllowed, PNew | reason: AI permission is your choice | You withdraw permission for Duet's AI: work in progress ends for good and nothing returns if you allow it again; your history, conversation and saved work stay (F3; Dev 2026-10-06).
%% event Duet publishes a new AI permission | by Duet | needs PAllowed | reason: only an AI permission you gave can go out of date | Duet asks you to allow a new version of what its AI does; your earlier consent never covers a use you haven't seen, so AI work pauses without being used up until you allow it (Dev 2026-10-25). Withdrawing instead means AI is not allowed.
%% event allow the new AI permission | by you | command on your AI settings: Allow the new version, clicked while DIn | needs PNew, TCur | reason: AI permission is your choice; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You allow the new version; paused work continues.
%% event turn AI off | by you | command on your AI settings: Turn off, clicked while DIn | needs SwOn, TCur | reason: the switch is yours; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You turn off Conversation and insights: AI work pauses without being used up, and your conversation stays readable (D7).
%% event turn AI on | by you | command on your AI settings: Turn on, clicked while DIn | needs SwOff, TCur | reason: the switch is yours; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You turn AI back on; paused work continues.
%% event pause proactive work | by you | command on your AI settings: Pause proactive work, clicked while DIn | needs PwOn, TCur | reason: the control is yours; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | One control pauses Duet's own work and the Reminders and Check-ins you asked for; chat and memory keep working (north-star.md, Requested follow-through).
%% event resume proactive work | by you | command on your AI settings: Resume proactive work, clicked while DIn | needs PwPaused, TCur | reason: the control is yours; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | Duet's own work, Reminders and Check-ins continue.
%% event Duet publishes new Terms | by Duet | needs not TNew | reason: newer Terms already waiting are replaced by the newest | Duet asks you to accept newer Terms; until you do, the app waits on them and AI work pauses without being used up (D7; Dev 2026-10-04). During setup you agree to the newest version.
%% event accept the new Terms | by you | command on your account: Accept the new Terms, clicked while DIn | needs TNew | reason: only your own agreement records the Terms | You accept the newer Terms and paused work continues.
%% event sign out on this device | by you | needs DIn | reason: commands need a session on this device | This device forgets your account and stops its notifications; your other devices and any practice connection are unchanged (north-star.md, sign-out).
%% event sign out everywhere | by you | needs DIn | reason: commands need a session on this device | Every session ends, here and on your other devices, which must sign in again; your account, history and any practice connection stay (ENG-161). Duet says done only once every session has ended (22780b06).
%% event sign in on another device | by you | needs not ANone, ADeleting | reason: another device joins an account that exists and isn't being deleted | You sign in to the same account on another device. The graph follows the account from this device, so the account starts here.
%% event sign out on another device | by you | needs ODIn | reason: only a signed-in device signs out | That device forgets your account.
%% event delete your account | by you | command on your account: Delete account, clicked while DIn | needs AAgree, AName, AChoose, AReady | reason: deletion is yours alone, once, for an account not already being deleted | After confirming who you are, Duet starts deleting everything it keeps about you and ends any practice connection (ENG-161, F2).
%% event the deletion finishes | by Duet | needs ADeleting | reason: only a started deletion finishes | Everything is gone from Duet and from every device; nothing old work or a restored backup does brings it back (ENG-161). A deletion still finishing is never shown as done.
%% event export your data | by you | command on your account: Export, clicked while DIn | needs AReady, ExNone, ExReady, ExFailed | reason: exporting is always yours, even before newer Terms, as deleting your account is (Dev 2026-10-26); one export is prepared at a time | You ask for everything Duet keeps about you; a new export replaces the last one (ENG-161).
%% event your export is ready | by Duet | needs ExPreparing | reason: only an export being prepared finishes | Everything Duet keeps about you is ready to save, each item with its source and date: the conversation and its runs with your feedback, your health records and readings, insights, Plans, Reminders and Check-ins, For my doctor, your doctor's plan, and your sources and connections (ENG-161; north-star.md, Source access, export and deletion).
%% event your export can't finish | by Duet's runtime | needs ExPreparing | reason: only an export being prepared fails | The export is never shown as ready when it isn't; you can ask again.
%%
%% The conversation: one continuous thread, like texting (Dev 2026-10-25: chat works like Muse and
%% Instinct). You can always type; a message you send while Duet writes steers that reply; there is
%% one Send and no Stop. A sent message is never lost (D1).
%% event type in the composer | by you | needs DIn, TCur | reason: the composer belongs to this device's session and a set-up account; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You write a draft; it waits while AI is off or permission is missing (north-star.md, Product structure).
%% event clear your draft | by you | needs DrText, TCur | reason: only a draft can be cleared; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You empty the composer.
%% event ask about this | by you | needs DIn, TCur | reason: only a set-up account has items to ask about; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You pick Ask about this on an insight, a record, a measurement or a saved item: that item joins your draft, your text stays, and nothing is sent (north-star.md, Today; ENG-26). While you draft it shows its current version, marked if it was corrected since you picked it; the message keeps the version it carried once sent (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event remove the attached item | by you | needs CtxOn, TCur | reason: only an attached item can be removed; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | The item leaves your draft.
%% event reply to a message | by you | needs DIn, TCur | reason: only a set-up account has a thread; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You quote one earlier message, yours or Duet's, in your draft; quoting gives no new permission to repeat what it said (north-star.md, Product structure).
%% event dismiss the quote | by you | needs QOn, TCur | reason: only a quote can be dismissed; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | The quote leaves your draft.
%% event send your message | by you | needs DIn, AReady, PAllowed, SwOn, TCur, DrText | reason: a message goes to Duet's AI, which needs your permission, the switch on and current Terms (F3) | Your words move into the outgoing message with what they carry, and the composer is empty for the next one.
%% event Duet receives your message | by Duet | needs OSending, OUnsure, AReady | reason: only a message on its way arrives, sent or not yet confirmed | Your message is in the thread for good. With no reply in progress Duet starts one; while Duet is writing, your message steers that reply, which answers both (Dev 2026-10-25).
%% event your message isn't confirmed | by the network | needs OSending | reason: only a message on its way can go unconfirmed | Duet can't tell yet whether it arrived; the message says so and keeps your words, never shown as failed or as sent.
%% event try sending again | by you | needs DIn, OUnsure, OUnsent, TCur | reason: only a message that didn't arrive or isn't confirmed is retried; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | The same message goes again; it can never arrive twice.
%% event Duet refuses your message | by Duet | needs OSending | reason: only a message on its way can be refused | A definite refusal: the message stays with your words, Try again and Edit.
%% event edit the unsent message | by you | needs DIn, OUnsent, TCur | reason: only a refused message goes back to the composer; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | Its words and quote return to the composer, after asking if they would replace a newer draft; its attached item returns at its current version.
%% event Duet finishes the reply | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: only a reply being written finishes | The reply is complete in the thread with what it cites.
%% event the reply can't finish | by Duet's runtime | needs RWriting | reason: only a reply being written can fail | What was written stays, marked unfinished, with Try again; never silence (D1). Whatever the reply already saved stays saved.
%% events Duet posts in the thread = Duet finishes the reply | the reply can't finish
%% events Duet has something to tell you = Duet proposes a note on its own | Duet finishes its own work with something to tell you | Duet delivers the Reminder | Duet delivers the Check-in | the Check-in can't finish | the Check-in keeps failing | your doctor's plan arrives or changes | your practice schedules your appointment | your practice moves your appointment | your practice cancels your appointment | your practice's invitation reaches you | your practice discharges you
%% events Duet noticed something on its own = Duet proposes a note on its own | Duet finishes its own work with something to tell you
%% events Duet stops writing early = turn AI off | Duet publishes new Terms | Duet publishes a new AI permission | withdraw AI permission
%% event you see the new messages | by you | needs ThUnseen, DIn, AppFront, TabDuet, CoNone, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation, TCur | reason: only messages on screen in front of you are seen; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first | The conversation shows Duet's new messages on this device's screen, so they are seen everywhere: seen is one fact for your account (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event you see the new messages on another device | by you | needs ThUnseen, ODIn | reason: only a signed-in device shows the conversation | You read Duet's new messages on your other device; they are seen here too (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event leave Duet | by you | needs AppFront | reason: only an app on screen goes to the background | Duet goes to the background on this device; anything in progress keeps going.
%% event open Duet | by you | needs AppBack | reason: only an app in the background comes back | Duet is on screen again, where you left it.
%% Alerts (north-star.md, Notifications; Dev 2026-10-26). Each message alerts once, like texting, while Duet is in
%% the background on a device whose alerts are allowed and that is signed in to your account. Replies, what you
%% asked for and your practice's news always alert there; what Duet noticed from its own work alerts only once you
%% turn on its one switch, which follows your account. Duet keeps no quiet hours of its own: your device's Focus
%% or Do Not Disturb decides whether an alert sounds. Lock-screen text is generic: no health value, source,
%% doctor content or medical claim; a Reminder may show the words you agreed. A notification never proves the
%% work behind it finished, and opening one starts nothing new.
%% event allow alerts | by you | needs NtAsk | reason: only the first ask is answered here | You allow Duet's alerts on this device when it first asks.
%% event don't allow alerts | by you | needs NtAsk | reason: only the first ask is answered here | Duet works the same without alerts; everything waits in the thread.
%% event turn alerts off in your device's settings | by you | needs NtOn | reason: only allowed alerts are turned off | This device stops getting Duet's alerts, and the notification waiting on it goes.
%% event turn alerts on in your device's settings | by you | needs NtOff | reason: only alerts that are off are turned on | This device gets Duet's alerts again from now on; nothing missed arrives late.
%% event turn on alerts for Duet's own work | by you | command on your alerts: Turn on, clicked while DIn | needs IaOff, TCur | reason: the choice is yours; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | Off until you turn it on (north-star.md, Notifications): what Duet noticed from its own work then alerts you too. One switch saved with your account, so every device follows it (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event turn off alerts for Duet's own work | by you | command on your alerts: Turn off, clicked while DIn | needs IaOn, TCur | reason: the choice is yours; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | What Duet noticed still posts in the thread, without alerting you.
%% event open the notification | by you | needs NoWaiting, AppBack | reason: only a notification waiting on this device opens, from outside Duet | Duet opens on the conversation at its newest message; it starts nothing new.
%% events Duet tells you what you asked for or your practice's news = Duet delivers the Reminder | Duet delivers the Check-in | the Check-in can't finish | the Check-in keeps failing | your doctor's plan arrives or changes | your practice schedules your appointment | your practice moves your appointment | your practice cancels your appointment | your practice's invitation reaches you | your practice discharges you
%% event try the reply again | by you | command on the reply: Try again, clicked while DIn | needs RUnfinished, PAllowed, SwOn, TCur | reason: Duet's AI needs your permission, the switch on and current Terms | Duet writes the reply again from your messages.
%% event Duet's AI sees a possible emergency or self-harm | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: only a reply being written can carry a safety line | Duet's AI judges that what you describe could be an emergency, or mentions self-harm.
%% event mark the reply helpful | by you | command on your feedback: Helpful, clicked while DIn | needs RDone, TCur | reason: only a finished reply takes feedback; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | 👍 saves at once, a quiet tapback; switching from 👎 drops its reasons and note (Dev 2026-09-23).
%% event mark the reply not helpful | by you | command on your feedback: Not helpful, clicked while DIn | needs RDone, TCur | reason: only a finished reply takes feedback; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | 👎 saves at once and offers optional reasons and a note.
%% event remove your feedback | by you | command on your feedback: Remove, clicked while DIn | needs RDone, TCur | reason: only a finished reply takes feedback; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | Tapping the chosen thumb again removes it, with its reasons and note.
%% event save the details | by you | command on your feedback: Done, clicked while DIn | needs FbDown, TCur | reason: only a 👎 takes reasons and a note; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | Done saves the reasons and note with your 👎; closing without Done keeps the 👎 alone. Your feedback stays in your account and never reaches the AI.
%%
%% Follow-through: Plans, Reminders and Check-ins you asked for (ENG-34). Duet saves them only from
%% your current message or a proposal you accepted; you edit, pause, resume or cancel them, in
%% conversation or directly. Duet's AI never resumes them. They continue through
%% inactivity. A Plan is a routine with no schedule.
%% event Duet saves the {kind} you asked for | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: a reply saves follow-through only from your current message or a proposal you accepted; reading a record or a provider's note adds no step, and nothing it read can ask for more than you did (Dev 2026-09-25; ENG-34, Dev 2026-10-25) | The {kind} is saved and shows on Today; the thread shows its receipt only once the save is confirmed (ENG-34).
%% event the {kind} comes due | by the clock | Its scheduled time arrives, in the timezone you agreed. A Reminder needs no AI, so at its time Duet delivers it, even while AI is off, newer Terms wait or a newer AI permission waits (Dev 2026-10-26). Any other time that comes while AI permission is withdrawn, or while a newer AI permission, AI off or newer Terms wait (for a Check-in), or proactive work is paused passes undelivered; nothing stale arrives later (F3; Dev 2026-10-25). A time that comes while the last Check-in couldn't finish replaces it.
%% event Duet starts the Check-in | by Duet | needs FuDue@checkin, PAllowed, SwOn, TCur, PwOn | reason: a Check-in is AI work and proactive work: it needs your permission, the switch on, current Terms and proactive work on (F3, D7, D10) | Duet's AI begins the Check-in from your current context; its accepted instruction is fixed.
%% event Duet delivers the Check-in | by Duet's AI | needs FuRun@checkin | reason: only a running Check-in delivers | Its result posts in the thread as Duet's message; a delivered Check-in never means you did something medical. After its last time the Check-in is completed.
%% event the Check-in can't finish | by Duet's runtime | needs FuRun@checkin | reason: only a running Check-in fails | What was written stays, marked unfinished, and Duet says so in the thread with Try again, since you asked for it; never silence (D1; Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event the Check-in keeps failing | by Duet's runtime | needs FuRun@checkin | reason: only a running Check-in fails | After failing repeatedly, it pauses itself and Duet says so in the thread; only you resume it (Dev 2026-10-26). How many failures in a row count as repeatedly is the runtime's (infrastructure-gaps.md).
%% event try the Check-in again | by you | command on the Check-in: Try again, clicked while DIn | needs FuStuck@checkin, PAllowed, SwOn, TCur, PwOn | reason: a Check-in is AI work and proactive work: it needs your permission, the switch on, current Terms and proactive work on (F3, D7) | Duet runs the same Check-in again with its accepted instruction.
%% events proactive AI work pauses = turn AI off | Duet publishes new Terms | Duet publishes a new AI permission | pause proactive work
%% event Duet delivers the Reminder | by Duet | needs FuSched@reminder, PAllowed, PNew, PwOn | reason: a Reminder needs no AI, but your consent and proactive work still govern it (north-star.md, Insight evidence; Dev 2026-10-26) | At its time, Duet posts it in the thread: your agreed words lead, unchanged, and with AI on Duet may add what it judges useful (Dev 2026-10-26). After its last time the Reminder is completed.
%% event pause the {kind} | by you | command on the {kind}: Pause, clicked while DIn | needs FuActive@{key}, {due}, {run}, {stuck}, TCur | reason: only a live {kind} pauses; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You pause it; a run in progress ends for good.
%% event resume the {kind} | by you | command on the {kind}: Resume, clicked while DIn | needs FuPaused@{key}, TCur | reason: only a paused {kind} resumes; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | It continues from its next time.
%% event change the {kind} | by you | command on the {kind}: Change, clicked while DIn | needs FuActive@{key}, {due}, {run}, {stuck}, FuPaused@{key}, TCur | reason: only a saved {kind} changes; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You change it directly; a run in progress ends for good (backend-architecture.md, Accepted follow-through).
%% event cancel the {kind} | by you | command on the {kind}: Cancel, clicked while DIn | needs FuActive@{key}, {due}, {run}, {stuck}, FuPaused@{key}, TCur | reason: only a saved {kind} is cancelled; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You cancel it; its receipt in the thread says so.
%% event Duet changes the {kind} as you asked | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: a reply changes follow-through only from your current message; what it read can't ask for more than you did (backend-architecture.md, Accepted follow-through; ENG-34) | The reply changes the {kind} as your message asked; a run in progress ends for good, and its receipt shows once the change is confirmed (ENG-34).
%% event Duet pauses the {kind} as you asked | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: a reply pauses follow-through only from your current message | The reply pauses the {kind} as your message asked; a run in progress ends for good. Only you resume it.
%% event Duet cancels the {kind} as you asked | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: a reply cancels follow-through only from your current message | The reply cancels the {kind} as your message asked; its receipt in the thread says so.
%% event Duet saves the Plan you asked for | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting | reason: a reply saves a Plan only from your current message (Dev 2026-09-25) | Your routine or checklist is saved, with no schedule and nothing automatic; saving again replaces its one current version.
%% event change the Plan | by you | command on the Plan: Save, clicked while DIn | needs PlSaved, TCur | reason: only a saved Plan changes; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You edit the Plan directly; asking in conversation saves it again.
%% event delete the Plan | by you | command on the Plan: Delete, clicked while DIn | needs PlSaved, TCur | reason: only a saved Plan is deleted; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | The Plan goes; Reminders and Check-ins that served it keep running (Dev 2026-09-28).
%% event Duet deletes the Plan as you asked | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting, PlSaved | reason: a reply deletes a Plan only from your current message | The Plan goes as your message asked; Reminders and Check-ins that served it keep running.
%% event Duet links the {kind} to your Plan as you asked | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting, PlSaved, FuActive@{key}, {due}, {run}, {stuck}, FuPaused@{key} | reason: a reply links follow-through only from your current message, to a saved Plan, for a {kind} you have (Dev 2026-09-28) | The {kind} now serves your Plan, and the Plan's detail shows it. A {kind} serves at most one Plan; you change the link in conversation, not with a new control.
%% event Duet unlinks the {kind} from your Plan as you asked | by Duet's AI | needs RWriting, LkPlan@{key} | reason: a reply changes the link only from your current message (Dev 2026-09-28) | The {kind} keeps running on its own.
%%
%% Duet's own work and Today. Duet may take something on whenever it judges it worth doing for you
%% (Dev 2026-10-26): a look at your day, a weekly recap, new records, a trend to follow. When and how
%% often is the harness's (infrastructure-gaps.md). Work may finish with something to tell you, posted
%% in the thread and pinned on Today, or quietly, and silence is success. Work running when what it
%% read changes looks again from a fresh snapshot.
%% Your health sources (ENG-162; behaviour-contract A, B, F1; north-star.md, Connect your health and
%% Source access): your phone's health data (Apple Health on iPhone, Health Connect on Android) and
%% Doctors & hospitals, where each organization you sign in to is authorized, refreshed, fails and is
%% disconnected on its own (B1). One organization stands for each. Records are kept exactly as sent
%% (B3); a record missing from a later import is never deleted (B4); while anything retries, what you
%% have stays visible (B6). Disconnecting stops new data and keeps everything already imported until
%% you delete your account (F1). A source that stops working shows it on the source, with Reconnect;
%% Duet's AI may mention it, and nothing else alerts you (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event connect a doctor or hospital | by you | needs DIn, AReady, OrgOff, TCur | reason: a set-up account connects; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first (north-star.md, Identity and setup) | You search for your hospital or clinic among the portals Duet can authorize end to end (Epic MyChart, Oracle Health and healow) and go to its portal to sign in (north-star.md, Connect your health).
%% event the portal signs you in | by the organization's portal | needs OrgSigning, OrgResigning | reason: only a sign-in in progress finishes, in the session that started it | You finish signing in at the portal and come back to Duet; the import starts. Reconnecting the same organization resumes the same history (F1).
%% event cancel the portal sign-in | by you | needs OrgSigning, OrgResigning | reason: only a sign-in in progress is cancelled | You back out of the portal; cancelling is never shown as a failure (north-star.md, Connect your health).
%% event the portal sign-in fails | by the organization's portal | needs OrgSigning, OrgResigning | reason: only a sign-in in progress fails | The portal doesn't sign you in; Duet says why, from one shared failure meaning, and you can try again.
%% event the import finishes | by Duet | needs OrgImporting | reason: only a running import finishes | Everything this import found is kept, with or without the source's own warnings (B5).
%% event the import finishes with items it couldn't read | by Duet | needs OrgImporting | reason: only a running import finishes | The import ends as partial: the records or pages it couldn't read are named with their reason, and everything else is kept; the next refresh tries them again (B2, B5; Dev 2026-10-04).
%% event the import can't finish | by the organization's portal | needs OrgImporting | reason: only a running import fails | The source is down or keeps failing; what you already have stays visible and the next refresh tries again (B5, B6).
%% event the organization stops accepting Duet's access | by the organization's portal | needs OrgConn | reason: only a connected organization can drop its access | The portal's sign-in expired or was revoked; the source shows it couldn't update since its last import, with Reconnect (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event refresh your records | by you | command on the organization: Refresh, clicked while DIn | needs OrgCurrent, OrgPartial, OrgTrouble, TCur | reason: only a connected organization that isn't already importing refreshes; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first | You ask for an update now; a stuck import elsewhere never blocks it (B6).
%% event your records refresh on their own | by Duet | needs OrgCurrent, OrgPartial, OrgTrouble | reason: only a connected organization that isn't already importing refreshes | Duet asks each connected organization for what changed, on its own; how often is the harness's (infrastructure-gaps.md, Health sources). A refresh you ask for never waits on it (B6, B7).
%% event reconnect the organization | by you | needs DIn, OrgSignIn, TCur | reason: only an organization that needs you to sign in again is reconnected; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first | You go back to the portal to sign in again; your history stays as it is.
%% event disconnect the organization | by you | command on the organization: Disconnect, clicked while DIn | needs OrgConn | reason: only a connected organization disconnects; stopping a source is always yours, even before newer Terms, as leaving your practice is (Dev 2026-10-26) | New data stops at once and work in flight is fenced; everything already imported stays, as of its last update, until you delete your account (F1).
%% event allow your phone's health data | by you | needs DIn, AReady, PhOff, TCur | reason: a set-up account connects; newer Terms wait for your acceptance first | You allow Duet to read Apple Health on iPhone or Health Connect on Android; declining changes nothing (ENG-162; north-star.md, Connect your health).
%% event your phone's history finishes importing | by your phone | needs PhImporting, DIn | reason: only an import in progress finishes, and the phone reads only while you're signed in on it (behaviour-contract rule 12) | The available history arrives in resumable steps, and any gap in coverage is stated (A5).
